K-One-Kernel: perbaiki build xm_power pada CONFIG_VIRT_CPU_ACCOUNTING_GEN

CONFIG_NO_HZ_FULL (patch 0008) secara otomatis memilih
CONFIG_VIRT_CPU_ACCOUNTING_GEN melalui baris "select" di kernel/time/Kconfig.
Sebelum itu simbol tersebut tidak aktif, sehingga seluruh blok
CONFIG_VIRT_CPU_ACCOUNTING_GEN di driver vendor xm_power.c dibuang oleh
preprocessor dan tidak pernah dikompilasi.

Ketika simbol aktif, task_cputime() versi GEN ikut aktif dan memanggil
vtime_delta(). Fungsi tersebut hanya ada sebagai helper "static" di
kernel/sched/cputime.c, tidak di-EXPORT, dan tidak dideklarasikan pada
header publik mana pun. Akibatnya build modul gagal dengan:

  xm_power.c:206:11: error: call to undeclared function 'vtime_delta';
  ISO C99 and later do not support implicit function declarations

Tambahkan salinan lokal helper tersebut, ditambah include yang dibutuhkan
(linux/vtime.h, linux/sched/clock.h, linux/seqlock.h), lalu arahkan call
site ke helper lokal. sched_clock() memang EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL sehingga
boleh dipanggil dari modul. Perilaku dan hasil perhitungan tetap sama
dengan implementasi di kernel/sched/cputime.c.
--- a/drivers/power/xm_power/xm_power.c
+++ b/drivers/power/xm_power/xm_power.c
@@ -1,5 +1,30 @@
 #include "xm_power.h"
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_VIRT_CPU_ACCOUNTING_GEN
+#include <linux/seqlock.h>
+#include <linux/sched/clock.h>
+#include <linux/vtime.h>
+
+/*
+ * vtime_delta() is a private helper of kernel/sched/cputime.c: it is static
+ * and never exported, so a module cannot reference it. Enabling
+ * CONFIG_NO_HZ_FULL selects CONFIG_VIRT_CPU_ACCOUNTING_GEN, which makes the
+ * task_cputime() branch below reachable and broke the build with
+ * "call to undeclared function 'vtime_delta'". Replicate the helper here.
+ */
+static u64 xm_vtime_delta(const struct vtime *vtime)
+{
+	unsigned long long clock;
+
+	clock = sched_clock();
+	if (clock < vtime->starttime)
+		return 0;
+
+	return clock - vtime->starttime;
+}
+#endif
+
+
 #ifdef pr_fmt
 #undef pr_fmt
 #endif
@@ -203,7 +228,7 @@
 		if (vtime->state < VTIME_SYS)
 			continue;
 
-		delta = vtime_delta(vtime);
+		delta = xm_vtime_delta(vtime);
 
 		/*
 		 * Task runs either in user (including guest) or kernel space,
